  "context_pill": "Direct Tax / Marginal Relief",
  "example_summary": "Marginal relief calculation for X Ltd. for A.Y. 2026-27",
  "source_provision": "| Category / Parameter | Statutory Condition / Benchmark | Tax Rate / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Domestic Company Basic Rate (Concessional Turnover)** | Gross receipts/turnover in PY ≤ ₹ 400 Crore | **25%** of Total Income |\n| **Domestic Company Basic Rate (Standard)** | Gross receipts/turnover in PY > ₹ 400 Crore | **30%** of Total Income |\n| **Surcharge Slab 1** | Total Income > ₹ 1 Crore but ≤ ₹ 10 Crore | **7%** of Basic Tax |\n| **Surcharge Slab 2** | Total Income > ₹ 10 Crore | **12%** of Basic Tax |\n| **Health & Education Cess** | Levied on (Basic Tax + Surcharge - Marginal Relief) | **4%** |\n\n### Core Statutory Checklist\n\n* **Marginal Relief Applicability**: Available whenever total income exceeds the surcharge threshold limit of ₹ 1 Crore or ₹ 10 Crore.\n\n* **Statutory Formula for Marginal Relief**:\n  $$\\text{Marginal Relief} = (\\text{Tax} + \\text{Surcharge on Total Income}) - [\\text{Tax on Threshold Limit} + (\\text{Total Income} - \\text{Threshold Limit})]$$\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Statutory Cap on Incremental Tax**: The tax payable (including surcharge) on income exceeding ₹ 1 Crore shall NOT exceed the tax payable on ₹ 1 Crore PLUS the amount of total income that exceeds ₹ 1 Crore.",
